            "The Shifting Bottleneck Procedure (SBP), originally formulated by Adams, Balas, and Zawack, represents one of the most powerful combinatorial optimization heuristics for job-shop scheduling. In a job shop containing $m$ machines and $n$ jobs, each job follows a unique, complex technological routing sequence with distinct processing times. The exact mathematical optimization of such environments represents an NP-hard problem; computing the globally optimal schedule via brute-force mixed-integer linear programming is computationally intractable for real-world enterprise scale. The Shifting Bottleneck Procedure circumvents this complexity by decomposing the complex job shop into $m$ individual single-machine scheduling sub-problems.",
